course: dictionary
lesson: 2852
title: One word, two worlds
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Venice was a merchant republic ruled by an elected Doge (a duke chosen for life) and councils of noble families.» Venice, republic and elected are the clues, so here Doge means a ruler.
explain: Online, doge means something very different. A picture of a Shiba Inu dog with silly broken English, like «much wow, very amaze», is a joke meme. If the words around doge are about a dog, a funny picture or a post, it is the meme, not the ruler.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense. A ruler of Venice does not fit a dog with silly spelling, and a meme does not fit a palace.
fact: The Doge was the elected ruler of Venice and Genoa, old city states in Italy, for about a thousand years until 1797.
fact: A Doge was chosen for life, not born into power.
fact: As an internet meme, doge is a joke picture of a Shiba Inu dog with funny broken English, such as «much wow, very amaze».
fact: Dogecoin is online money that started as a joke based on this meme.
fact: Context clues such as Venice, a palace or a dog picture tell you which meaning of doge the writer means.
exercise: «Venice was a merchant republic ruled by an elected Doge.» What is a Doge? | A type of boat | *A ruler of Venice | A famous painter
exercise: A friend posts a picture of a Shiba Inu saying «much wow, very amaze». What is doge here? | *A joke internet meme | A kind of bread | A ruler of Genoa
exercise: Which word in the Venice sentence tells you the Doge was chosen by others? | *elected | Venice | merchant
test: «The Doge ruled Venice for about a thousand years.» Until which year did the Doge rule? | 1979 | 1497 | *1797
test: Dogecoin is online money that started as a joke. What was it based on? | A mountain in Italy | *A Shiba Inu meme | A Venetian palace
exam: Ava reads «much wow, very amaze» in a story about a dog. Which meaning of doge fits best? | A ruler of Venice | A large rowing boat | *A joke internet meme of a dog
